VS Code slice 2: workstation subscription CLI bridge (person start only)

Fixed the macOS assertion to compare the recorded cwd with `await realpath(folder)`. Every other assertion and all production code remain unchanged. Updated and checked the required handoff. No migrations or merge performed.

## PR description

Implements a person-started, PAT-only pull transport at `/api/v1/companion`, reusing BER-298’s companion package and the existing subscription CLI adapters.

Claims use `SKIP LOCKED` with a 60-second lease renewed by heartbeat. Lifecycle events are posted in order, keyed by sequence and fingerprint. Cancellation is written to the ledger first, then returned on heartbeat; the worker stops the CLI session through the registry. The hosted dispatcher and sweeper skip companion runs. The envelope contains neither the PAT nor provider credentials.

Settings and companion connections cannot replace each other. A new companion ID cannot replace a connection with a live run lease; replacement is allowed after lease expiry.

Out of scope: simultaneous Settings and companion connections, which require a forward migration in a separate issue; remote, SSH and WSL workspaces; vscode.dev; automatic bridge startup.

